# Cursor Rules for ALOUTE

Before generating or modifying any code in this project:
1. Always read skills/INDEX.md first to locate the owner file for the feature/bug.
2. Read the designated file in skills/:
   - skills/domain_system.md: Domain entities, business logic, constraints, schema, WHO CAN DO WHAT.
   - skills/system_architecture.md: ApiResponse envelope, pagination, error codes, HTTP status.
   - skills/aloute-openapi.yaml: Exact API paths, query params, schemas (do NOT invent custom endpoints).
   - skills/backend_rule.md: Spring Boot conventions, layers (Controller -> Service -> Repository), transactions, JPA.
   - skills/author_rule.md: Spring Security, JWT, authentication, authorization.
   - skills/frontend_rule.md: Thymeleaf, Bootstrap, JavaScript conventions.
   - skills/docker_reverse_proxy_rule.md: Docker, Docker Compose, Nginx reverse proxy.
3. Principle: ONE RULE -> ONE OWNER -> ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
